                <pb facs="0283" n="189" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg189"/>

                <head>No. 151.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Denby to Mr. Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-02-18"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 18, 1887</date>.
                        (Received April 12.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 311.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that the first
                    installment of the amount agreed to be paid on account of the losses of the
                    Methodist Episcopal mission at Chungking, 5,000 taels, was paid by the local
                    authorities at the time agreed on.</p>
                <p>It has been received by Mr. Frank S. Gamewell, superintendent of the mission.</p>
                <p>1 have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Denby</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
